<h3 id="6-differences-between-implicit--explicit-animations">6. Differences between implicit &amp; explicit animations</h3>

<p>Implicit animations always exist; to disable them, you must set a flag.
Explicit animations don’t exist; to make one explicit, you have to enable it.</p>

<p>Just observe the result after the animation finishes executing.
For example: a simple UIView frame movement — if it moves from point A to point B, and upon completion returns to the original position, that’s an implicit animation.</p>

<p>Core Animation is explicit animation, because it can animate layer properties directly and also override default layer behavior.</p>

