<h3 id="10-when-are-images-decoded-and-how-to-optimize">10. When are images decoded, and how to optimize</h3>

<p>Decoding happens when loading into memory: from UIImage -&gt; CGImage -&gt; CGImageSourceCreateWithData(data) to create an ImageSource and turn it into a bitmap. All this work is done by Core Animation while the image is loaded into memory, stored in the backingStore, and decoded before being sent to the GPU pipeline for processing.</p>

<h4 id="how-to-optimize">How to optimize</h4>

<p>Manually operate the image encoding APIs yourself —</p>

<p>the CGImageSource family. Based on sensible timing and use of operating system resources, tune out a library with small caching and fast loading.</p>

<p>See the open-source <a href="https://github.com/pinterest/PINRemoteImage">PINRemoteImage</a> or <a href="https://github.com/ibireme/YYWebImage">YYWebImage</a></p>

